# UNINTENTIONAL FLIGHT INTO ICING CONDITIONS (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decisions 2026-10-23 and 2026-10-27): the heading, the italic sub-heading, every item, action and both CAUTION blocks as printed. The row marks are the letters A to I of the AFM page that was compared. ASSUMPTION for the owner: the booklet may print numbers 1 to 9 instead; the marks are plain data (the `number` fields), so swapping them is one edit per row plus the typed table in tests/checklist-reference.ts. Row A (leave the icing area) and row I (ATC) have no panel action and stay lines: the icing area ends by itself after a fixed time, further actions come with the physics phase. Cabin heat ON is TEMPERATURE at 75 or WARM, the same rule as the warm air that melts the ice; Cabin air DEFROST is DIRECTION at DEFROST; the POWER row is an increase of the POWER lever; the Emergency windows row is optional, as printed "if required". All other text is own wording. The ice growth, the length of the icing area, the onset window and the cue bound are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: icing-unintentional
title: ICING CONDITIONS
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03-35 UNINTENTIONAL FLIGHT INTO ICING CONDITIONS
  verified: "2026-10-27"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: cloud
briefing:
  situation: "You are flying in cloud when ice begins to form on the windscreen. No message is shown on the primary flight display. The ice builds up on both halves of the windscreen, and the pitot heating, the cabin heat and the alternate air and static sources are not in use."
initial:
  controls:
    sw.pitot_stall_heat: "off"
    lv.env_temp: cold
    lv.env_direction: face
    lv.alt_air: closed
    lv.alt_static: closed
  quantities:
    ice_pilot: 15
    ice_copilot: 15
parameters:
  ice_accretion: 0.5
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: Unintentional Flight Into Icing Conditions
procedure[12]:
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: Unintentional Flight Into Icing Conditions
  - kind: line
    number: A
    text: Leave the icing area (by changing altitude or turning back in order to reach zones with a higher ambient temperature).
  - kind: group
    id: grp_pitot
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: pitot_heat_on
        severity: critical
        number: B
        text: PITOT/STALL HEAT
        action: "ON"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.pitot_stall_heat
          is: "on"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_cabin_heat
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: cabin_heat_on
        severity: critical
        number: C
        text: Cabin heat
        action: "ON"
        done:
          check: state_in
          control: lv.env_temp
          in[2]: t75,warm
  - kind: group
    id: grp_cabin_air
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: cabin_air_defrost
        severity: critical
        number: D
        text: Cabin air
        action: DEFROST
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.env_direction
          is: defrost
  - kind: group
    id: grp_power
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: power_increase
        severity: standard
        number: E
        text: POWER lever
        action: increase power, in order to prevent ice build-up on the propeller blades apply power changes periodically
        done:
          check: travel_rel
          control: lv.power
          op: gt
          delta: 0
  - kind: group
    id: grp_alt_air
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: alt_air_open
        severity: critical
        number: F
        text: ALTERNATE AIR
        action: OPEN
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.alt_air
          is: open
  - kind: group
    id: grp_alt_static
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: alt_static_open
        severity: critical
        number: G
        text: Alternate static
        action: OPEN
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.alt_static
          is: open
  - kind: group
    id: grp_windows
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: windows_open
        severity: optional
        number: H
        text: Emergency windows
        action: open if required
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_window
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    style: caution
    text: ICE BUILD-UP INCREASES THE STALLING SPEED.
  - kind: comment
    style: caution
    text: WHEN THE PITOT HEATING FAILS EXPECT LOSS OF AIRSPEED INDICATION.
  - kind: line
    number: I
    text: ATC
    action: advise if an emergency is expected
# The ice shows on both halves of the windscreen; the slow cue gets its own bound (lint L23), an instructor-review value. The icing area ends by itself (the icing exposure of the aircraft physics).
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  message_within_s: 24
  cues[2]: ice_pilot_side,ice_copilot_side
